-    // CORNER_GRACE_MS: see genuineDivergence Case A below.
-    // SAME_GOAL_CLOSE_GAP: sameGoal alone is a discrete TUPLE match (JOINER's
-    // first step happens to target the same tile MASTER is currently
-    // targeting) — it does NOT by itself prove the two are actually close
-    // together. A pair that starts a genuine, natural one tile apart can
-    // legitimately share that exact tuple for their very first mutual step
-    // (both about to walk the same corridor), which used to be read as
-    // proof of same-position join intent and collapsed the real one-tile
-    // gap to a full overlap. The approved strict boundary is expressed in
-    // logical route tiles: <=0.10 may earn SAME_POSITION, >=0.15 is
-    // immediately too late, and the narrow 0.10-0.15 ambiguity band gets at
-    // most 100ms to return to the close side before defaulting to TRAILING.
-    // These are native, direction-normalized gaps; render corrections never
-    // feed back into the decision.
-    // A close pair must remain close for one complete native movement interval
-    // before SAME_POSITION is allowed to become authoritative. This prevents
